 "buyers_guide": [
  {
   "q": "What does a smart relay do?",
   "a": "It hides behind a wall switch, inside a fan canopy, or in an appliance and switches the power, so you keep your existing switch and add smart control. Dry-contact relays can also trigger garage doors, gas fireplaces, and boilers."
  },
  {
   "q": "Do I need a neutral wire?",
   "a": "Most relays do. Check your switch box for a bundle of white wires before buying. A few models work without a neutral, and the table notes which."
  },
  {
   "q": "Is it safe to install myself?",
   "a": "Only if you're comfortable with household wiring and turn the breaker off first. If you're not sure, have an electrician install it. Never exceed the relay's amp rating."
  }
 ],
